# fixedbugs, defect 556, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C2; the
# critic's `onedef`).
#
# A header defines `twice`, neither `static` nor `inline`, and two modules
# bind it, so each module's unit compiles a definition of it. Until
# 2026-10-10 the link refused the program at exit 2, *internal error:
# linking failed: duplicate symbol '_twice'*, the compiler blamed for the
# header. Told at exit 1 before anything links, naming the header and the
# modules, with the remedy C offers.
use fixedbugs556/also

extern "fixedbugs-556-defines.h"
    function twice(x: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_defined_twice

function main()
    print(twice(x: 3))
    print(also.doubled(x: 4))
